      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few options for a polite and professional rejection email. You can choose the one that best fits your company's tone!\n\nOption 1 (Warm and Direct): \"Thank you so much for investing your time in our interview process for the Senior Dev role. We truly enjoyed learning about your experience, and the final decision was incredibly difficult. We have decided to move forward with another candidate whose specific background aligned slightly closer to our immediate needs at this time. We wish you the very best in your job search and future endeavors.\"\n\nOption 2 (More Formal): \"We appreciate you taking the time to interview for the Senior Developer position. The caliber of candidates was very high, which made our final selection process challenging. While your skills are impressive, we have selected a candidate whose profile matched a unique set of requirements for this particular role. We wish you success in finding a role that is a perfect fit for your talents.\"\n\nOption 3 (Brief and Kind): \"Thank you again for making it to the final round for the Senior Dev role. We were very impressed with your technical abilities. After much consideration, we have decided to proceed with a different candidate. We hope you keep us in mind for future opportunities that might be",
